---
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { join } from "node:path";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const upstreamLicense = readFileSync(join(process.cwd(), "LICENSES", "models.dev-MIT.txt"), "utf8");
const ownLicense = readFileSync(join(process.cwd(), "LICENSE"), "utf8");
---

<Base title="Licensing" description="Licences and attribution for the providers.dev dataset and the models.dev data it builds on.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Licensing and attribution</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The baseline of this catalog is imported from <a href="https://models.dev">models.dev</a> (<a href="https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev">source</a>), which is published under the MIT
      License. providers.dev is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by models.dev or by any provider listed here.
    </p>

    <h2>What is whose</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every provider and entry whose <code>providers_dev.origin</code> is <code>upstream</code> comes from models.dev, except the fields listed in its <code>providers_dev.provenance</code>.</li>
      <li>Everything under a <code>providers_dev</code> key, every entry whose origin is <code>added</code>, and every field listed in a <code>provenance</code> array is ours.</li>
      <li>Measurements come from <a href="https://github.com/ngvoicu/cache-ttl-probe">cache-ttl-probe</a> (MIT).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>That marking is kept through every export, so a consumer of <code>/api.json</code> can always tell the two apart.</p>

    <h2>Using this data</h2>
    <p>
      Our additions, corrections and code are under the MIT License below. If you redistribute the dataset, keep both notices. The dataset ships with them:
      <a href="/data/LICENSE-models.dev.txt"><code>/data/LICENSE-models.dev.txt</code></a> and <a href="/data/NOTICE.txt"><code>/data/NOTICE.txt</code></a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Model and provider names are trademarks of their owners and are used only to identify them. The data is provided as is; check a provider's own documentation before relying on a limit.
    </p>

    <h2>models.dev licence</h2>
    <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap">{upstreamLicense}</pre>

    <h2>providers.dev licence</h2>
    <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap">{ownLicense}</pre>
  </div>
</Base>
